      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the commit message keep the two points from the PS15 thread that got lost in the rewrite? First, what fails without the patch: in a 4KB process, `mmap()` of a (1 + 2^n) × 4KB ring, the size perf tools compute from the page size, fails with `-EINVAL`. Second, why the data PTEs can map a different slice from the one `vma_slice_offset()` gives (the data starts one 4KB page into the VMA, but at slice 0 of its kernel page), and why that\u0027s fine: the VMA is `VM_IO | VM_PFNMAP` with no `-\u003eaccess`, so GUP, `__access_remote_vm()` and coredumps never read through these PTEs.\n\nIt would also help to say what 4KB processes see now: a 4KB `data_offset`, and `-EINVAL` for 4KB and 8KB data rings. And could the subject mention 4KB processes, e.g. \"ANDROID: P3S: perf: Map a 4KB user page for 4KB processes\"?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "79e3bfc0b74d0c29c1f4a3a6e4321aae69e80ab1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
