      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T18:53:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would you mind folding the three `#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` blocks of this header into one, with the stubs in its `#else` branch? `perf_mmap_page_size()` and `perf_set_mmap_page_size()` each have a block inside the function, and `perf_map_main_p3s()` has a third. Something like:\n\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE\nstatic inline unsigned long perf_mmap_page_size(struct perf_buffer *rb)\n{\n\treturn rb-\u003emmap_page_size;\n}\n/* perf_set_mmap_page_size(), perf_map_main_p3s(), new helpers */\n#else\nstatic inline unsigned long perf_mmap_page_size(struct perf_buffer *rb)\n{\n\treturn __PAGE_SIZE;\n}\n/* their stubs */\n#endif\n```\n\nThe `#ifdef` around `mmap_page_size` in `struct perf_buffer` is fine as it is, since its accessors live here. Also, `PAGE_SIZE_KERNEL` in `perf_map_main_p3s()` would make the units explicit, as in the other P3S headers.",
