      "message": "Agreed that the 4KB layout needs this: `vmf-\u003epgoff` counts kernel pages, so upstream\u0027s check would also let the first three data slices become writable. Would you mind moving the 4KB case into `include/linux/p3s/perf.h` as well, so that upstream\u0027s check stays as it is? Something like:\n\n```\n\tif (vma_is_p3s_4k(vmf-\u003evma))\n\t\treturn p3s_perf_mmap_pfn_mkwrite(vmf);\n\n\t/* The first page is the user control page, others are read-only. */\n\treturn vmf-\u003epgoff \u003d\u003d 0 ? 0 : VM_FAULT_SIGBUS;\n```\n\nThe helper would allow only the first 4KB of the main ring (`!vma-\u003evm_pgoff`), with a stub in the header\u0027s `#else` branch.",
