      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T18:53:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for dropping the AUX mapping. A few rewrites from it seem to be left, and as far as I can see they give the same answers as upstream. `mmap_offset` here is `vm_pgoff \u003c\u003c PAGE_SHIFT`. `perf_mmap_aux()` already requires `aux_pgoff \u003d\u003d vm_pgoff`, so in `perf_mmap_open()` every VMA with a non-zero `vm_pgoff` is the AUX one. And `data_page_nr(rb)` in `perf_mmap_close()` is `perf_data_size(rb) \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT`. Would it be OK to drop those changes? I think the page size check at the top of this function isn\u0027t needed either, since AUX keeps the native layout whichever mm maps it, but I may be missing a case.\n\nThe `perf_data_size(rb) + perf_mmap_page_size(rb)` bound doesn\u0027t change anything on arm64, where AUX offsets and data sizes are whole kernel pages. Under x86_64 page size emulation, though, it becomes data + 16KB instead of data + 4KB. That looks right for the emulated metadata area, but like the accounting fix, could it move to aosp/4399088 (with `__PAGE_SIZE`)?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "79e3bfc0b74d0c29c1f4a3a6e4321aae69e80ab1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
