      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T18:53:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for moving the mapping into `include/linux/p3s/perf.h` and for requiring 16KB of data. I think the size checks could become a one-line accessor too. The only P3S difference is the 4KB user page, which is still backed by one kernel page. If `perf_mmap()` counts it as that kernel page, upstream\u0027s checks here and in `perf_mmap_rb()` work unchanged. Something like:\n\n```\n/* Count the 4KB user page of a 4KB process as the kernel page behind it. */\nstatic inline unsigned long p3s_perf_mmap_size(struct vm_area_struct *vma)\n{\n\tunsigned long size \u003d vma-\u003evm_end - vma-\u003evm_start;\n\n\tif (!vma_is_p3s_4k(vma) || vma-\u003evm_pgoff)\n\t\treturn size;\n\treturn size - mm_pte_size(vma-\u003evm_mm) + PAGE_SIZE_KERNEL;\n}\n```\n\nwith only this left here:\n\n```\n\tvma_size \u003d p3s_perf_mmap_size(vma);\n```\n\n`vma_size !\u003d PAGE_SIZE * nr_pages` then rejects data that isn\u0027t a multiple of 16KB, `perf_mmap_rb()` rejects page counts that aren\u0027t a power of two, and `user_extra` stays data + 1 kernel pages, which matches `perf_mmap_close()`. The `data_size` and `mmap_offset` locals, the re-indented checks and the `user_extra` and `nr_pages` change in `perf_mmap_rb()` could then go. Its page size check and `perf_set_mmap_page_size()` would stay. (`mmap_offset` is always `vm_pgoff \u003c\u003c PAGE_SHIFT` here anyway, since `vma_slice_off()` is rejected above.)",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "79e3bfc0b74d0c29c1f4a3a6e4321aae69e80ab1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
