      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the upstream helpers stay where they are? `perf_data_size()` moves into the P3S header unchanged, so upstream changes to it (`ring_buffer.c` uses it too) would land in a P3S file. Including `\u003clinux/p3s/perf.h\u003e` after it would keep it here, and the header could include `\u003clinux/page_size_compat_defs.h\u003e` itself, rather than `internal.h`.\n\nSimilarly, I think `perf_map_main_p3s()` can call `perf_mmap_to_page()`: it returns `__perf_mmap_to_page()` for every offset below `aux_pgoff`, and the AUX area starts after the main ring. `__perf_mmap_to_page()` could then keep its name and stay `static`, and the `ring_buffer.c` change and the `perf_mmap_main_page()` prototype could go.",
